\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Comparison with cancellation conditions}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Lüscher assumes that the cubes of the charges of the left-handed
Weyl fermions sum to zero in his construction of an Abelian chiral gauge
theory \citet{Equation (1.1), printed p. 1}{luscher1998abelian}.
For Weyl fermions in three space dimensions and one time dimension,
Hsieh gives separate conditions for the two cyclic symmetry types recalled in \ref{fdip-014N}.
These source results are cited, not proved here. The condition in
\ref{fdip-015D} concerns the coefficient functional of a fixed family
of finite operators. Its exponent is linear in their charges weighted
by their kernel indices. It yields no gauge-anomaly cancellation criterion.}
